---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = 'October 30, 2026';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Rank Labs" description="How Rank Labs collects, uses and shares information from getranklabs.com visitors and customers, including analytics, advertising pixels and the site chat.">

<section class="pt-32 pb-20 px-6">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-sm text-cyan-300 font-mono mb-4">LEGAL</div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Privacy <span class="gradient-text">Policy</span></h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-10">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-muted leading-relaxed">

      <div>
        <p>
          This policy explains what Rank Labs, LLC collects when you use
          <strong class="text-white">getranklabs.com</strong>, why we collect it, and who else
          sees it. We have written it in plain terms rather than legal boilerplate, because a
          policy you cannot read is not disclosure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Rank Labs, LLC is an SEO, GEO and ASO platform based in Orlando, Florida, United
          States. For any privacy question, contact
          <a href="mailto:hello@getranklabs.com" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">hello@getranklabs.com</a>
          or call <a href="tel:+14077438964" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">(407) 743-8964</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">What we collect</h2>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">When you fill in a form</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Our contact and signup forms collect the name, email address, business name, website
          URL, plan interest and any notes you choose to enter. Submissions are emailed to us and
          a record of the submission is stored so we can measure which pages produce enquiries.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">When you use the site chat</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Chat messages are stored so the conversation survives a page reload, and are relayed to
          us through Telegram so we can answer in real time. Alongside the messages we store the
          page you started from, your browser user-agent, a coarse location derived by our host
          (city, region and country only, never a precise location), and a one-way salted hash of
          your IP address used solely to rate-limit abuse. We do not store your IP address itself.
          If you give us an email address so we can follow up, we store that too. Conversations
          close automatically after 30 minutes of silence.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">How you found us</h3>
        <p class="mb-4">
          When you arrive, your browser records in its own session storage the referring site, the
          page you landed on, and any campaign parameters in the link such as utm_source or gclid.
          This is sent with a form submission so we know which channel produced the enquiry. It is
          cleared when you close the tab.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-2">Automatically, as you browse</h3>
        <p>
          Like any website, our host records standard request logs. We also run the analytics and
          advertising tools described below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Analytics and advertising</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          <strong class="text-white">Google Analytics 4</strong> measures which pages are read and
          which links are used. It assigns your browser a random identifier stored in a cookie. It
          does not receive your name or email address from us.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          <strong class="text-white">The Meta pixel</strong> reports page views and completed
          contact-form submissions to Meta so we can measure whether our Facebook and Instagram
          advertising works, and so we can show ads to people who have visited the site. It sets
          cookies and can be matched by Meta to a Facebook or Instagram account you are signed
          into. The form contents themselves are not sent to Meta — only the fact that a
          submission happened, and the page it happened on.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-2">You can switch these off independently of us:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 ml-5 list-disc">
          <li>
            Google Analytics —
            <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">install Google's opt-out add-on</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Meta —
            <a href="https://www.facebook.com/adpreferences/ad_settings" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">adjust your Meta ad settings</a>.
          </li>
          <li>Any browser — block third-party cookies, or use a content blocker. The site works normally with both blocked.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">How we use what we collect</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 ml-5 list-disc">
          <li>To answer your enquiry and deliver the services you asked for.</li>
          <li>To measure which pages and which advertising campaigns produce enquiries.</li>
          <li>To protect the site from spam and abuse.</li>
          <li>To meet our legal and accounting obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with anyone for their
          own marketing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Who else processes your data</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">We use these providers to run the site and the business:</p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-white text-left">
                <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Provider</th>
                <th class="py-3 font-semibold">What it handles</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">Cloudflare</td><td class="py-3">Hosting, request logs, the database holding form and chat records</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">Google</td><td class="py-3">Analytics</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">Meta</td><td class="py-3">Advertising measurement and audiences</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">Resend</td><td class="py-3">Delivering form submissions to us by email</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">Telegram</td><td class="py-3">Relaying site-chat messages to us so we can reply</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">Stripe</td><td class="py-3">Payments. Card details go directly to Stripe; we never receive or store them</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We may also disclose information where the law requires it, or to establish or defend a
          legal claim.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Form submissions and the records behind our reporting are kept while we are doing
          business together and afterwards for as long as we need them for tax, accounting and
          legal purposes. Chat transcripts are kept as a record of the conversation. Ask us to
          delete any of it and we will, except where we are required to keep it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Wherever you live, you can ask us what we hold about you, ask for a copy, ask us to
          correct it, or ask us to delete it. Email
          <a href="mailto:hello@getranklabs.com" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">hello@getranklabs.com</a>
          and we will respond.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are a California resident, the CCPA as amended gives you the rights to know,
          delete, correct, and to opt out of sale or sharing. We do not sell personal information.
          Because the Meta pixel can be treated as "sharing" for cross-context behavioural
          advertising, you can opt out by blocking it using any of the methods above, and we will
          not discriminate against you for doing so.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Children</h2>
        <p>
          This is a business-to-business service. It is not directed at children under 13 and we
          do not knowingly collect their information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of the page. Material
          changes will be announced to active customers by email.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gradient-border rounded-2xl p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Rank Labs, LLC · Orlando, Florida, United States<br />
          <a href="mailto:hello@getranklabs.com" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">hello@getranklabs.com</a>
          · <a href="tel:+14077438964" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">(407) 743-8964</a>
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
